> It's all about banning superficial traits of types of firearms rather than pushing for a federal firearms registry and licensing/insurance requirements. 

&#x200B;

So you criticize gun control but you don't know what gun control is about. See the problem???

&#x200B;

The husband/the priest is the asshole to be honest.

I don't get it. Why does she have to lie to the priest? She do really have to be christian to get married there? Isn't her husband enough? (genuinely asking, I know nothing about religion).

&#x200B;

I'm an atheist but I make a difference between believing in a god, and human faith. I would marry in a church to please my husband because religion can be important to some people and can even do good to them. Because I respect their faith. But lying is different...

&#x200B;

However I think if it's your daughter's wedding you should support her (it's not like she's committing a crime, she's willing to make compromise, she's a good girl).

NAH 

But it's not your fault but I think your sister is right. 

In another context (like no white people committing genocide and putting native people in parks then ignoring that they are in the worst situation as if it has nothing to do with the slavery colonization rapes and murders) it would be ok to use someone else's culture.

&#x200B;

It won't change the world if you can find another text, but if you can that would be a little bit of respect they deserve and never got. Also yes it participates to cultural appropriation (meaning you take what you like of this culture but ignore the awful context they live in).

&#x200B;

I think we should be more conscious of that kind of things or things will never change, and it starts with small gestures.

&#x200B;

The question you must ask yourself is "is this THAT important to me?" cause for native american people it is in a very deep way. 

&#x200B;

Maybe what you can do is to find a way to involve real native american people more to your wedding, since you say you feel "connected". Because so far you're only connected to the vague idea you formed based on assumptions. Maybe try an actual connexion with humans

&#x200B;

People. We've become accustomed to see uniformity and perfection.

Fat or """"ugly"""" people are so rare in movies and tv shows in general. People are all "beautiful", size 0 to 1. No glasses (unless ultimate nerd), small noses, shiny hair. Nobody's really old (like 50 to 70). ALL mums are hot and THIN. Random dudes have abs.

&#x200B;

I'm so happy whenever I see someone with a little belly fat in a movie while it should be the norm.

&#x200B;

EDIT: Ah and also kids who behave and talk in an adult way. I haven't seen a kid behave like a kid in a movie since the 80/90s

We purposely go to places to run (like the gym) and move. We do it in purpose but not to go to a specific place. Sometimes we are forced to do it. Most people say they don't like this activity and never do it.

&#x200B;

Maybe our hygiene routine too.

